From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ludovic Henry <git@ludovic.dev>
Date: Mon, 21 Sep 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] dtool: add riscv64 platform detection

dtool_platform.h's DTOOL_PLATFORM #if/#elif chain enumerates every arch it
builds on (linux_aarch64, linux_amd64, linux_i386, linux_arm, linux_ppc,
linux_e2k, ...) with no riscv64 case, so it falls through to the
unconditional #error at the bottom: "Can't determine platform; please
define DTOOL_PLATFORM in Config.pp file." The immediate next build error
(pandaSystem.cxx:300, "DTOOL_PLATFORM was not declared") is the same root
cause - the macro was never defined - not a separate problem.

Add a riscv64 branch alongside the other linux_* ones, matching their
shape (one #elif per arch, keyed on the compiler's own arch macro).
__riscv is defined by both GCC and Clang on every RISC-V target;
__riscv_xlen distinguishes the 64-bit ABI from rv32.

Upstream-Status: To upstream [not yet submitted; needs a riscv64 CI leg upstream doesn't have yet to validate against]

Signed-off-by: Ludovic Henry <git@ludovic.dev>
---
 dtool/src/dtoolbase/dtool_platform.h | 3 +++
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+)

diff --git a/dtool/src/dtoolbase/dtool_platform.h b/dtool/src/dtoolbase/dtool_platform.h
index ad2f857..0a75c75 100644
--- a/dtool/src/dtoolbase/dtool_platform.h
+++ b/dtool/src/dtoolbase/dtool_platform.h
@@ -68,6 +68,9 @@
 #elif defined(__aarch64__)
 #define DTOOL_PLATFORM "linux_aarch64"

+#elif defined(__riscv) && __riscv_xlen == 64
+#define DTOOL_PLATFORM "linux_riscv64"
+
 #elif defined(__x86_64)
 #define DTOOL_PLATFORM "linux_amd64"

--
